    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d30">

                <pb facs="0037" n="33" xml:id="pg33"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00/1371: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-05-09T14:00:00-04:00">May 9, 1939—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>120. A telegram of May 8 from the American Embassy at Berlin<anchor n="33"
                        xml:id="d30-f1"/> reads in part as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“German sources indicate that the proclamation of the German-Italian
                            military alliance as well as the reported conversations with Russia are
                            maneuvers intended to frighten the Western Powers and to influence Japan
                            to join Italy and Germany in a military alliance.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
